From ea73297c636c3660f9eb8bd353a1926d3f9940bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:09:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] video: sun5i-eink: rework to a palette-mode V4L2 scanout
 driver

The driver now only scans out complete 8bpp palette-indexed frames
composed in userspace: DEBE runs in palette mode (256 x u32 pin-state
table at BE+0x4400, uploaded via a private ioctl together with the
TCON timing parameters), and buffers are exchanged zero-copy through
a V4L2 output device (vb2, MMAP + DMABUF, EXPBUF for PRIME import
into the GPU). Queued frames scan back-to-back with no gaps; on an
empty queue scanout pauses at a frame boundary and resumes on the
next queued buffer. The kernel-side NEON composer and the custom
cdev interface are gone.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
